-- title:
--   Degree of level Mℓ over level M along q↦ q^ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $M$ and $\ell$ with $M\neq 0$ and $\ell$ prime, and a further nonzero natural number $M'$ with $M'=M\ell$. For a nonzero level $N$, write $F_N=\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull }N$ for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$) generated by the set of all $\mathtt{qExpand }\mathbb{Q}\,d\ \mathtt{jq}$ with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $N$, where $\mathtt{qExpand }\mathbb{Q}\,d$ is the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by multiplying all exponents by $d$, i.e. the substitution $q\mapsto q^{d}$. Let $\varphi\colon F_M\to F_{M'}$ be a ring homomorphism such that for every $f\in F_M$ the Laurent series underlying $\varphi f$ equals $\mathtt{qExpand }\mathbb{Q}\,\ell$ applied to the Laurent series underlying $f$. The conclusion is that $F_{M'}$, regarded as a module over $F_M$ through the algebra structure determined by $\varphi$, has finite rank equal to $\ell$ if $\ell\mid M$, and to $\ell+1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the degree formula $[\Gamma_0(M):\Gamma_0(M\ell)]=\psi(M\ell)/\psi(M)$ in its function-field form: the full modular function field of level $M\ell$ has degree $\ell$ or $\ell+1$ over the image of the level-$M$ field under the degeneracy substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$. Phrasing the larger level as a free variable $M'$ with $M'=M\ell$, and characterising the embedding only by its effect on $q$-expansions, lets it be applied to degeneracy pairs and flatness computations on Igusa-type schemes, which cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_modularFunctionFieldFull_mul_prime_eq_of_coe_eq_qExpand.lean

